# S07-T03: Org Handbook — Totem Governance (header rules)

## Objective

Project-agnostic company page: Totem header governance rules every app inherits.

## App-agent preflight (MANDATORY before code)

- [ ] MCP preflight — WARN if `:3000` down
- [ ] `explain("organization-planning")` + `explain("layer-cascade")`
- [ ] `get-file` — `organization/app/app.config.ts` (`agents` block for role names)
- [ ] `list-pages` category `company` — avoid nav/filename collisions
- [ ] `get-page` — read `docs/content/2.company/0.index.md`, `1.handbook.md` for tone

## Implementation

- [ ] Create `docs/content/2.company/2.totem-governance.md`
- [ ] Content (from `totem-v6/index.ti` axioms — paraphrase for humans, no `.ti` syntax):
  - **AI-only approval:** never simulate human LGTM/Go
  - **Role separation:** PLANNER plans, PM executes — same session must not do both
  - **Gating:** execution OPEN until literal `Go`/`LGTM` in latest user message
  - **Physical lock:** `gate: OPEN` on `.pd` is unexecutable until human opens
  - **Sprint home:** plans live in totem instance; work-control orchestrates
- [ ] Link agent roles to `organization/app/app.config.ts` `agents` block (names from `get-file`)
- [ ] Include **MCP preflight** subsection: start docs :3000, use `explain` before coding
- [ ] No app-specific paths (no todo; work-control one sentence max)

## Done when (app-agent tools)

- [ ] `get-page("/company/totem-governance")` — page exists via MCP
- [ ] `explain("organization-planning")` still consistent with new page
- [ ] Page readable without knowing which app is being built
